      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a question here: `friendly_name` is passed in by the user, so we can not guarantee that it is unique. However, mDNS requires `instance_name` to be unique. In mDNS, conflict resolution procedure is used to guarantee this (in current OSP implementation, if an instance name is already used, a sequence number will be added to the instance name to form a new instance name),\n\nSo there is such a situation: user pass in `friently_name\u003dTestName` but it is used already. so what users actully use is `TestName2`. Will this cause confusion to users?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 549,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 549,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "10eaca6995e48f7c343b26c17d96943259a317d1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
