      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T18:30:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a good question.  This is the way DNS-SD service advertisement has worked for a long time for printers and other devices.\n\nThere is nothing preventing two distinct agents from giving themselves the same display name and thus introducing a conflict in both the DNS-SD instance name and the `display-name` provided through the `agent-info` message.  Unless we want to change how display/instance names are assigned, the best we can do is to flag this situation in the UI.\n\nFiled https://github.com/w3c/openscreenprotocol/issues/358 to discuss possible spec changes.",
